    <section id="correlation" class="article-section">
      <div class="article-heading">
        <span>05.2 · independent emitters</span>
        <h2>No privileged process has to relay the whole story.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="telemetry-emitters">
        <article><small>emitter 01</small><strong><code>dekopond</code></strong><span>message · session · model · shell</span></article>
        <i aria-hidden="true">traceparent →</i>
        <article><small>emitter 02</small><strong><code>dekopon-brokerd</code></strong><span>authorization · provider · HTTP</span></article>
        <i aria-hidden="true">OTLP ↘</i>
        <article><small>backend</small><strong>OpenObserve</strong><span>joins by trace and parent IDs</span></article>
      </div>

      <p>The client sends optional W3C <code>traceParent</code> beside the proposal. The broker validates it and uses it only for span parenting. It never affects identity, Cedar, routing, replay protection, credentials, or durable audit.</p>

      <div class="invariant-notes">
        <article><span>W3C</span><h3>Telemetry trace ID</h3><p>Joins spans across processes and expires with trace retention.</p></article>
        <article><span>Dekopon</span><h3>Durable trace ID</h3><p>Correlates invocations and audit records independently of telemetry.</p></article>
        <article><span>strict</span><h3>Malformed context</h3><p>Rejects decoding rather than attaching broker work to a trace that does not exist.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="signals" class="article-section">
      <div class="article-heading">
        <span>05.3 · one job per signal</span>
        <h2>Audit, traces, and logs answer different questions.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="truth-label-cards">
        <article><div><span class="almanac-status almanac-status-current"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>Broker audit</span></div><h3>What was authorized?</h3><p>An owner-only hash-linked JSONL chain records identity, decision, policy IDs and digest, credential name, effect, outcome, and bounded evidence.</p></article>
        <article><div><span class="almanac-status almanac-status-current"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>OTel traces</span></div><h3>What ran, and where did time go?</h3><p>Spans preserve duration, parentage, safe identifiers, outcomes, and the path from chat to HTTP.</p></article>
        <article><div><span class="almanac-status almanac-status-current"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>OTel logs</span></div><h3>What should survive a sampled trace?</h3><p>Accounting, refusals, errors, lifecycle facts, and explicitly enabled transcript payloads remain searchable under separate retention.</p></article>
      </div>

      <div class="article-callout callout-warning">
        <strong>Telemetry is not authorization evidence.</strong>
        <p>A backend may sample, expire, reject, or lose telemetry. Broker authorization and hash-linked audit continue independently.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="logs" class="article-section">
      <div class="article-heading">
        <span>05.4 · logs that earn their storage</span>
        <h2>A span measures time. A log preserves a fact.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="comparison-table-wrap">
        <table class="almanac-table strategy-table">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Event</th><th scope="col">Why it is a log</th><th scope="col">Safe fields</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row"><code>accounting.model.turn</code></th><td>Cost must survive trace sampling and expiry.</td><td>duration, counts, reported token usage, outcome</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><code>accounting.http.request</code></th><td>Outside calls consume quota and budget.</td><td>method, authority, status, byte counts, outcome</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">refusal and error events</th><td>Operators need durable searchable failure categories.</td><td>stable category and bounded IDs, never raw error text</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><code>agent.model.*</code></th><td>Optional transcript text is too large for span attributes.</td><td>full payload only after explicit opt-in</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>Start/completed log pairs are absent because a span already has a start, duration, parent, and outcome. Logs do not become a noisier copy of the waterfall.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="privacy" class="article-section">
      <div class="article-heading">
        <span>05.5 · metadata first</span>
        <h2>See the flow without exporting the conversation.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="comparison-table-wrap">
        <table class="almanac-table strategy-table">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Included by default</th><th scope="col">Excluded by default</th><th scope="col">Never revealed by payload mode</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>service, agent, model, provider, capability IDs</td><td>chat messages, prompts, and model answers</td><td>model and provider credentials</td></tr>
            <tr><td>durations, counts, outcomes, token usage</td><td>model-authored scripts and tool output</td><td>OTLP authorization headers</td></tr>
            <tr><td>command kind, argument count, exit code</td><td>command arguments and provider input/output</td><td>HTTP headers and response bodies</td></tr>
            <tr><td>HTTP method, host, status, byte counts</td><td>URL paths and queries</td><td>credential values in audit or evidence</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p><code>telemetryPayloads: true</code> opts selected messages, scripts, provider input, and URLs into telemetry. It widens data, never authority or secret exposure. Durable audit remains metadata-only.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="openobserve" class="article-section">
      <div class="article-heading">
        <span>05.6 · open standards on small hardware</span>
        <h2>Send OTLP to the backend you choose.</h2>
      </div>

      <pre><code><span class="code-purple">export</span> OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:5080/api/default
<span class="code-purple">export</span> OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS='Authorization=Basic%20[REDACTED],organization=default,stream-name=dekopon'

<span class="code-comment"># Each process exports its own leg.</span>
dekopond --config /etc/dekopon/dekopond.yaml
dekopon-brokerd --config /etc/dekopon/broker.yaml</code></pre>

      <p>Dekopon supports OTLP over HTTP or gRPC. The repository’s OpenObserve smoke test starts a real receiver, executes a provider, searches trace and log streams, verifies correlation, and proves a sentinel input stayed out of both.</p>

